# GitHub CLI for Actions and CI

When asked to check GitHub Actions runs, workflow status, CI failures, PR checks, or run logs, use the **GitHub CLI (`gh`)** — not the REST API or web fetch.

## Commands

```powershell
gh run list --limit N
gh run view <run-id>
gh run view <run-id> --log-failed
gh run view --job=<job-id>
gh pr checks
gh pr view <number> --json statusCheckRollup
```

## Windows PATH fallback

On this machine, `gh` is installed at `C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe`. Cursor agent shells may not have it on PATH. If `gh` is not recognized:

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe" run list --limit 2
```

Prefer plain `gh` when it works; use the full path only when `Get-Command gh` fails.

## Repo context

- Remote: `https://github.com/elinorv2506/ai-assisted-qa-automation-2`
- Workflow: `.github/workflows/e2e.yml` (E2E Tests)

## Do not

- Use `WebFetch` or unauthenticated GitHub API calls when `gh` can answer the question
- Assume `gh` is missing without trying the full Windows path first
